# Cloudflare Pages headers for tracker.goinwardout.com
# The catalog files are large (~4 MB total) and change only when the ETL
# reruns — let browsers keep them for a day; Cloudflare's edge cache +
# brotli handle the rest. App code revalidates hourly so pushes show up.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# App code must always revalidate: there is no content hashing in the file
# names, so any positive max-age pins visitors to stale (possibly buggy) code
# until it expires. Revalidation is a cheap 304 via Pages' ETags.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Catalog data is large and changes only on ETL rebuilds; an hour of browser
# cache + ETag revalidation after that is the right trade.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
